## HOLDS
**Datasec only.** The product on screen is "Policy Designer" (C-62); any word you report uses it; no client or sample-client name or abbreviation in any file you write into the project. **Nothing to any human** (the reviewer, HP, the project owner's contacts); no mail, chat or card; replies to Tuesday only, through STATUS. No data change beyond the deploy: no engagement, answer, render, generate, submit, version number, governance record or secret-local decision created; no content release change; Guided stays OFF; no write to the demo through the browser. **Never delete** (quarantine; the only removals are the runbook's key strip, the NSG rule, your own VM `/tmp/b1608-*` files and the `b1608_restoretest` database, each backed up or named). Kill any process you start by port and cwd, never by name. Never force-push; every Datasec GitHub commit goes through CodeQL: never bypass, never dismiss an alert; no PR, no merge, no commit; `2_Project_Files`: read-only git verbs, every fetch in your scratchpad clone. **No records write:** no CLARIFICATIONS, BACKLOG, `history.md` or `JIRA.md` edit, no records branch, no Jira write; STATUS and evidence stay untracked in `Briefs/`. **PARTITION, your side:** you touch `HPSM-DEV-RG` / `hpsm-demo-vm` / `hpsm-demo-vmNSG`, your scratchpad, and `Briefs/2026-11-16_B1608_*`. **PARTITION, the other side:** Tuesday and the other seats do not touch the Composer demo, its group, the project's `Briefs/` B1608 files or the heavy lock while you run; the Composer VM is the only resource you open and no other project's `az` state is yours. Secrets never printed, copied or screenshotted; scan STATUS and `Briefs/2026-11-16_B1608_evidence/` for the site password, the demo host, the temp key, a private-key header, `eyJ`, `sig=`, `Bearer [A-Za-z0-9]`, a bcrypt hash and any stored text from the database: 0, with a planted control that fires. Shell: never `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (the project path has spaces and `!`); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a 